# Everything that must never be published lives under private/ or decomp/:
#   Valve's firmware + updater (copyrighted), USB captures (contain the full image),
#   decompiler output (a derivative of Valve's firmware), and unredacted notes/photos.
# Readers get the originals from their own Steam install: docs/firmware-format.md has the
# path and SHA-256 hashes.
private/
decomp/

# --- Safety net: Valve files or derivatives that land somewhere else by mistake ---
# Firmware images and the updater
*.fw
PROTEUS_FW_*
IBEX_FW_*
hardwareupdater.exe
hardwareupdater.cfg
# What tools/pyi_extract.py produces from the updater bundle
*.code
*.marshal
*.pyz
*.pyd
*.dll
*.exe
base_library.zip
# USB captures (contain the full firmware image and device serials)
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.cap
# Raw images, dumps and build outputs
*.bin
*.hex
*.elf
*.map
# Ghidra projects and decompiler exports
*.gpr
*.rep/
*.lock
*.lock~
*decompiled*
# ...and what the other tools/Ghidra*.java scripts write, plus a naming table built from them
*_named.c
*_named.csv
functions*.csv
xrefs.tsv
strings.txt
names.json

# --- Local working files ---
# Claude Code's working context (personal notes, not part of the write-up)
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
# Zephyr / build directories (for the future firmware)
build/

# Built release files (uploaded to GitHub Releases, not committed)
release/
